{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-leading-terms","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:leading-terms","kind":"definition","title":"Leading monomial, coefficient, and term","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-monomial-basis"],"tags":["groebner-basis","algebra"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.UnitalGroebner.LeadingTerm","text":"leading-terms.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/leading-terms.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:leading-terms\"></a><p>Assume that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> is well-ordered by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">&#x3C;</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f \\in A</code>, then we may write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code>\nuniquely as the finite sum:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">f = c_1 b_1 + c_2 b_2 + \\cdots + c_n b_n \\quad \\text{for } c_i \\in R^* := R \\setminus \\{0\\},\\; b_i \\in B</code></pre>\n<p>such that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_1 > b_2 > \\cdots > b_n</code>. Then:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>leading monomial</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\LM(f) := b_1</code></li>\n<li>The <strong>leading coefficient</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\LC(f) := c_1</code></li>\n<li>The <strong>leading term</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\LT(f) := \\LC(f) \\cdot \\LM(f)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>We say that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in B</code> <strong>divides</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code> (written <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\mid f</code>) if there are\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u, v \\in B</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\in R^*</code> such that\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\LT(u \\cdot \\beta \\cdot v) = \\LT(f)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/leading-terms.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"2.2.3"}
